    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen `vim.ui.open()` is called with a URL that includes an ampersand (`&`) in the query string, the browser opens only the part before the first `&`. For example:\n\n```lua\nvim.ui.open(\"https://duckduckgo.com/?q=hello&t=brave\")\n```\n\nThe browser opens `https://duckduckgo.com/?q=hello`, and the `&t=brave` parameter is lost.\n\nCalling `:wait()` on the returned `SystemObj` reveals:\n\n```\n=vim.ui.open(\"https://duckduckgo.com/?q=hello&t=brave\"):wait()\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```lua\n{\n  code = 1,\n  signal = 0,\n  stderr = \"'t' 不是内部或外部命令，也不是可运行的程序\\n或批处理文件。\\n\",\n  stdout = \"\"\n}\n```\n\n*(Translation of the stderr line: `'t' is not recognized as an internal or external command, operable program or batch file.`)*\n\nThis stderr output appears even though the command executed (as shown in the `SystemObj._state.cmd`) is:\n\n```\n{ \"cmd.exe\", \"/c\", \"start\", \"\", \"https://duckduckgo.com/?q=hello&t=brave\" }\n```\n\nDespite the error, the browser does launch but shows the truncated URL.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start Neovim with `nvim --clean`.\n2. Execute `:lua vim.ui.open(\"https://duckduckgo.com/?q=hello&t=brave\")`.\n3. Observe the URL opened in the default browser.\n4. Optionally, call `:lua =vim.ui.open(\"https://duckduckgo.com/?q=hello&t=brave\"):wait()` to see the exit code and stderr.\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe full URL (`https://duckduckgo.com/?q=hello&t=brave`) should be opened.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1328+g2edb1c0009\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows 11\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWezterm\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\ngithub assets nightly",
